      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"shifting the weight\" doesn't change the fact that the void is still there. i've been thinking about it logically lately. if the universe is indifferent and nothing we do has a permanent impact, then the value of existing vs not existing is basically zero. it's like a zero-sum game. if the outcomes are mathematically equal, then choosing to leave isn't even a \"bad\" choice, is it? it's just a neutral one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
